    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d863">

                <pb facs="0823" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/766</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Helsingfors</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Haynes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d863-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1917</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 6, 11.10
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The president Finland Senate to-day before Diet proclaimed Finland free republic.
                    He asks me to ascertain if the United States of America will recognize Finland
                    as independent state and if so may government send delegates to lay their point
                    of view before our Government.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d863-f2"/> I learn from
                    reliable sources that Swedish-Germans [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] urging
                    Germany immediately to recognize Finland independence. Only our prompt
                    recognition will prevent Germany from securing firm sympathy and domination in
                    eastern Baltic. Names of delegates will be referred to me for approval. After
                    having consulted French and English colleagues they are dispatching similar
                    wires to their Governments and Embassies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thornwell Haynes</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d863-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d863-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador in Russia in telegram No. 1890, Dec. 8, 5 p.m., with
                    instructions: “Advise Department your views fully and at earliest
                    opportunity.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d863-f2" n="2" xml:id="d863-f2-content">
                <p>Answered Dec. 8: “Matter under consideration.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
